    <string name="manual_h_home">Home</string>
    <string name="manual_home">Add, reorder and remove tabs in Settings &gt; Home. Tap a tab to change its list style (list/grid, artwork, lines 1 and 2, sort order) and the levels down to the tracks. With a single tab, the tab row is hidden.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_now_playing">Now playing</string>
    <string name="manual_now_playing">Choose the items and their order in Settings &gt; Now playing. Tap the artwork to open the album, or the artist to open the album artist\'s albums. Swipe down to go back to the previous screen, like the down arrow at the top left. Format shows the codec, bit depth and sample rate; ReplayGain shows the gain being applied. The shuffle button cycles through off → by track → by album (with a disc mark) → off. The ⋮ menu at the top right adds the track to a playlist, goes to its album or artist, or shows track info.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_album_flow">Album Flow</string>
    <string name="manual_album_flow">Swipe the covers or turn the wheel below to choose an album. Tap the center cover (or the center of the wheel) to open it, and MENU for more actions. With the order set to Random, the albums are shuffled each time you open the tab.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_album_order">Album order</string>
    <string name="manual_album_order">Settings &gt; Home sets the album order for all artists. Album order in the menu at the top right of an artist\'s album list sets an order for that artist only, including a manual order. When you change the common order, you can keep or clear the per-artist settings.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_rg">ReplayGain</string>
    <string name="manual_rg">Track gain: the track value (or the album value if missing).\nAlbum gain: the album value (or the track value if missing).\nAuto: album gain when listening through an album, track gain when shuffling or mixing.\nThe gain is applied digitally inside the app; the system volume is not used. Clipping prevention limits the gain to 1/peak. Changes take effect immediately, even for the track that is playing.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_library">Library</string>
    <string name="manual_library">Only the music folders you add (and their subfolders) are read. Press Scan after changing their contents; the app does not scan on start. With \"Music files only\" access, APE, DSD, WavPack and M3U files may be hidden; allow \"All files access\" to see them. With .nomedia respected, folders containing a .nomedia file are skipped. Gapless playback is always on, and playback pauses when headphones are unplugged.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_tags">Tag rules</string>
    <string name="manual_tags">Multiple values are separated by \";\" by default. You can add separators (space-separated), but adding \"/\", \",\" or \"&amp;\" would split names such as AC/DC. Multi-value fields are tag names separated by spaces (e.g. ARTIST ALBUMARTIST COMPOSER GENRE). Match \"Ignore leading articles\" to your MusicBee setting. The join separator is used when several artists are shown on one line.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_templates">List text</string>
    <string name="manual_templates">Lines 1 and 2 can combine these fields: %1$s\nExample: &lt;Artist&gt; — &lt;Year&gt;\nAn empty line 1 shows the name; an empty line 2 shows nothing.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_playlists">Playlists</string>
    <string name="manual_playlists">Long-press a track or album and choose Add to playlist. From the menu at the top right of an album or artist screen, you can add all tracks at once, or pick them with checkboxes. Import M3U/M3U8 files exported from MusicBee in Settings &gt; Library, and add path rules to convert Windows paths (e.g. D:\\Music\\ → /storage/XXXX-XXXX/Music/).\nFrequently played is built automatically from your listening and updates by itself. Listening to at least half of a track counts as a play; moving on earlier counts as a skip. Recent listening counts more.</string>
    <string name="manual_h_search">Search</string>
    <string name="manual_search">Hiragana/katakana, full-width/half-width and upper/lower case are treated alike. Separate words with spaces to find items that contain all of them. Sort tags are searched too.</string>
